/* book Worked example: Q: An airliner flies an approach at a ground speed of 140 kt with a vertical speed of 750 ft/min down. Its overhead HUD has an exit aperture of D = 150 mm, and the pilot's eye is L = 600 mm from it. (a) Find the flight path angle γ, where the FPV sits below the horizon line. (b) Find the instantaneous field of view. (c) Is the FPV inside the instantaneous field of view when the pilot looks along the horizon?
   1. Ground speed in ft/min: 140 kt × 101.27 = 14 178 ft/min.
   2. Flight path angle: γ = arctan(750 ÷ 14 178) = arctan(0.0529) = 3.03°. The FPV is drawn 3.03° below the horizon line, on the usual 3° glide path.
   3. IFOV = 2 arctan(150 ÷ (2 × 600)) = 2 arctan(0.125) = 2 × 7.125° = 14.25°.
   4. Half of the IFOV is 7.13° above and below the line of sight.
   5. 3.03° is less than 7.13°, so the FPV is inside the instantaneous field of view.
   Answer:  */
