/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - ARINC 429 runs on a shielded twisted pair.
   - Only one transmitter may drive a pair, and up to 20 receivers listen.
   - Tw is the time per word including the minimum 4-bit gap, in seconds; R is the bit rate in bit/s.
   - MIL-STD-1553B runs at 1 Mbit/s on a shielded twisted pair, with each box joined to the main cable by a transformer-coupled stub.
   - One bus controller (BC) starts every transfer.
   - In a receive transfer (BC to RT) the BC sends the command and the data words, and the RT answers with its status word.
   - ARINC 429 suits one box broadcasting many values to many users, such as an air data computer feeding displays. 1553B suits many boxes that must talk both ways with confirmation, such as the mission computer, radar and stores management of a
   - Answer. 0.36 ms per word and 2778 words/s maximum; the load is 28.8 % at high speed; at low speed it would need 230 % of the bus, so it does not fit; the parity bit is 1.
   - Answer.
*/
