/* book Worked example: Q: An air data computer sends on one ARINC 429 bus: 12 labels at 50 times a second and 20 labels at 10 times a second. Each word is followed by the minimum 4-bit gap. (a) Find the word time and the maximum word rate at high speed (100 kbit/s). (b) Find the bus load. (c) Would the same traffic fit at low speed (12.5 kbit/s)? (d) The first 31 bits of one word contain fourteen 1s. What is bit 32?
   1. High speed: Tw = 36 ÷ 100 000 = 0.36 ms. Maximum rate = 1 ÷ 0.00036 = 2778 words/s.
   2. Traffic: 12 × 50 + 20 × 10 = 600 + 200 = 800 words/s.
   3. Load at high speed: 800 ÷ 2778 = 0.288, that is 28.8 % (check: 800 × 0.36 ms = 288 ms in each second).
   4. Low speed: Tw = 36 ÷ 12 500 = 2.88 ms; maximum rate = 347 words/s. 800 words/s is 800 ÷ 347 = 2.3 times the capacity, so it does not fit.
   5. Parity: fourteen 1s is even, so bit 32 must be 1 to make fifteen, an odd number.
   Answer:  */
