/* book Worked example 2: Q: On a 1553B bus the BC asks an RT to transmit 4 data words (RT to BC). The RT replies after 8 µs, and the BC leaves 4 µs before the next message. (a) Find the message time. (b) Show that a receive message with 4 data words takes the same time. (c) The BC polls 8 such RTs every 10 ms. Find the bus load.
   1. Word time: 20 bits ÷ 1 Mbit/s = 20 µs.
   2. Transmit message: command 20 µs, response gap 8 µs, status 20 µs, 4 data words 80 µs, then 4 µs to the next message: 20 + 8 + 20 + 80 + 4 = 132 µs.
   3. Receive message: command 20 µs, 4 data words 80 µs, response gap 8 µs, status 20 µs, gap 4 µs: also 132 µs. Both have one command, n data and one status word.
   4. Load: 8 × 132 µs = 1056 µs in each 10 000 µs, that is 10.6 %.
   Answer:  */
